<title>USA: FOB Gulf Grain - Corn values rise, SRW wheat weak.</title>
<headline>FOB Gulf Grain - Corn values rise, SRW wheat weak.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Gulf FOB corn basis values were higher in reaction to exporters needing grain to cover existing sales, grain dealers said.</p>
<p>Dealers said light farmer selling of corn and soybeans has shippers scrambling for supplies.</p>
<p>Soft red winter wheat values were lower in reaction to light export demand, dealers said. Hard red winter wheat values were unchanged.</p>
<p>Tunisia is scheduled to tender overnight for 100,000 tonnes of optional origin wheat for January and February shipment.</p>
